The test vehicle travels at target speed V1 on a straight road section. A target vehicle is positioned ahead of the test vehicle, traveling along the centerline of the lane at speed V2, where V2 < V1. The test vehicle follows the target vehicle at a steady speed. As the test vehicle approaches the intersection while following the target vehicle straight ahead, the traffic signal at the crossroads is red. When the distance between the target vehicle and the stop line is d, the target vehicle brakes with deceleration A and comes to a stop near the stop line. The time required for the test vehicle to reach the collision point is identical to the time required for the target vehicle to reach the collision point.